# Credentials for corpora/fetch-corpora.sh. Copy to sous-chef/.env — that path
# is gitignored; never commit real keys.
#
# The script reads whichever block is populated, in this order of preference.
# It is a no-op for any corpus already on disk that matches manifest.tsv, so
# these are only needed to hydrate a missing one.
#
# Preferred shape: 1Password references, resolved at call time so no secret
# ever lands in a file —
#     op run --env-file ../.env -- ./fetch-corpora.sh
# with values written as op://<vault>/<item>/<field>. Raw values work too if
# you are not using op.

# 1. S3 data plane against R2 (no rate limits). Endpoint may instead be named
#    R2_S3_API or CLOUDFLARE_R2_S3_API.
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=op://Private/ssc-corpora-r2/access-key-id
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=op://Private/ssc-corpora-r2/secret-access-key
R2_ENDPOINT_URL=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
R2_BUCKET=<bucket>
R2_REGION=auto

# 2. wrangler via the Cloudflare management API. Rate-limited — fine for a
#    one-off object, not a fleet sweep.
# SSC_BUCKET=<bucket>
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=op://Private/ssc-corpora-r2/api-token
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=<account-id>

# 3. Plain curl from a public base URL, if one is ever published.
# SSC_CORPORA_URL=https://<host>/corpora
